    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="integrity-mark" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="integrity-axis integrity-axis-v"></span>
          <span class="integrity-axis integrity-axis-h"></span>
          <span class="integrity-core"></span>
        </div>

        <div class="container hero-inner">
          <p class="eyebrow">Brand Integrity by Design</p>

          <h1>
            Restoring Integrity
            <br />
            and Beauty to the Open Web.
          </h1>

          <p class="hero-subtitle">
            Behavioral Integrity. Data Integrity. Better Advertising.
          </p>

          <p class="hero-copy">
            The future of advertising should not depend on more tracking,
            more intermediaries, or more impressions. It should depend on
            verifiable participants, verifiable information, and advertising
            experiences people actually value.
          </p>

          <div class="metrics">
            <div class="metric">
              <div class="metric-label">Average CTR</div>
              <div class="metric-value">15%</div>
            </div>

            <div class="metric">
              <div class="metric-label">Peak CTR</div>
              <div class="metric-value">70%+</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <a
            class="hero-metrics-source"
            href="#case-study"
          >
            JiJi Style proof of concept <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container">
          <p class="eyebrow">01 — The Problem</p>

          <h2 class="section-title">
            The Open Web Has an Integrity Problem
          </h2>

          <p class="lead">
            Programmatic advertising has created enormous efficiency,
            but today's advertising ecosystem often rewards scale and volume
            more than user experience, content quality, and long-term brand value.
          </p>

          <div class="problem-grid">
            <article class="card">
              <h3>Excessive Advertising Infrastructure</h3>
              <p>
                Modern webpages can carry extensive advertising auctions,
                measurement systems, trackers, and third-party scripts in
                addition to the content users actually requested.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
              <h3>User Migration to Ad Blocking</h3>
              <p>
                Users increasingly protect themselves through browser-level
                privacy tools and ad blocking, weakening the economic
                relationship between quality publishers and their audiences.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
              <h3>Fraud and Unverifiable Participants</h3>
              <p>
                Bots, crawlers, intermediaries, and automated systems operate
                at enormous scale while their identities and intentions are
                often difficult to verify.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="vision" class="section belief">
        <div class="container">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 — Our Belief</p>

          <div class="belief-layout">
            <div class="belief-intro">
              <h2 class="section-title">
                Brand Integrity
                <br />
                by Design
              </h2>

              <p class="lead">
                A healthy digital ecosystem requires integrity in both
                how organizations behave and how digital information is
                created, published, and maintained.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="integrity-diagram">
              <div class="integrity-circle behavioral">
                <div>
                  <h3>Behavioral<br />Integrity</h3>
                  <p>Integrity of the actor</p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="integrity-circle data-circle">
                <div>
                  <h3>Data<br />Integrity</h3>
                  <p>Integrity of the information</p>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="brand-result">
                <span>Behavior + Data</span>
                <strong>Brand Integrity</strong>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="integrity-principle">
            <div>
              <span>Behavioral Integrity</span>
              <strong>How do you act?</strong>
            </div>

            <div class="plus">+</div>

            <div>
              <span>Data Integrity</span>
              <strong>Can your information be verified?</strong>
            </div>

            <div class="equals">=</div>

            <div class="brand">
              <span>The Result</span>
              <strong>Brand Integrity</strong>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="approach" class="section index-section">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="index-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">03 — Solution</p>

              <h2 class="section-title">
                Brand Integrity Index
              </h2>
            </div>

            <p class="index-intro">
              Brand Integrity should not be an abstract promise.
              We propose a measurable framework for evaluating integrity
              from two complementary dimensions:
              <strong>behavior and data.</strong>
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="index-grid">
            <article class="index-column behavioral-index">
              <div class="index-column-heading">
                <span class="index-number">01</span>

                <div>
                  <p class="index-type">Behavioral Integrity</p>
                  <h3>Does the originator act with integrity?</h3>
                </div>
              </div>

              <ol class="index-list">
                <li>
                  <span class="item-number">01</span>
                  <div>
                    <strong>Clear Originator Identity</strong>
                    <p>
                      The organization clearly identifies who is responsible
                      for the content and digital property.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>

                <li>
                  <span class="item-number">02</span>
                  <div>
                    <strong>Transparent Policies</strong>
                    <p>
                      Editorial standards, privacy policies, and other relevant
                      policies are publicly available.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>

                <li>
                  <span class="item-number">03</span>
                  <div>
                    <strong>Transparent Corrections &amp; Deletions</strong>
                    <p>
                      Meaningful corrections, updates, and deletions are
                      publicly disclosed.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>

                <li>
                  <span class="item-number">04</span>
                  <div>
                    <strong>Responsible Advertising &amp; Data Practices</strong>
                    <p>
                      Advertising and data practices respect users and the
                      wider digital environment.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>
              </ol>

              <p class="index-note">
                These observable signals can increasingly be evaluated by AI,
                creating the potential to assess Behavioral Integrity at scale.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="index-column data-index">
              <div class="index-column-heading">
                <span class="index-number">02</span>

                <div>
                  <p class="index-type">Data Integrity</p>
                  <h3>Can the published information be verified?</h3>
                </div>
              </div>

              <ol class="index-list">
                <li>
                  <span class="item-number">01</span>
                  <div>
                    <strong>Authenticity of the Originator</strong>
                    <p>
                      The identity behind digital information can be
                      technically verified.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>

                <li>
                  <span class="item-number">02</span>
                  <div>
                    <strong>Integrity of Articles &amp; Text</strong>
                    <p>
                      Unauthorized modification of published text can be
                      detected.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>

                <li>
                  <span class="item-number">03</span>
                  <div>
                    <strong>Provenance of Images &amp; Video</strong>
                    <p>
                      The origin and history of visual media can be
                      technically evaluated.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </li>
              </ol>

              <div class="technology-note">
                <span>IMPLEMENTATION EXAMPLES</span>

                <p>
                  Open technologies and standards such as <strong>Originator Profile (OP)</strong> and
                  <strong>C2PA</strong> provide examples of technical
                  approaches that can support these forms of Data Integrity.
                </p>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="index-conclusion">
            <p>Two dimensions. One measurable objective.</p>
            <strong>Brand Integrity</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section advertising-model">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="model-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">04 — The Advertising Model</p>

              <h2 class="section-title model-title">
                <span>One Page</span>
                <span class="model-times">×</span>
                <span>One Advertiser</span>
              </h2>
            </div>

            <div class="model-message">
              <p class="model-kicker">Brand Integrity in Practice</p>

              <p>
                What if a webpage stopped competing for attention
                and started protecting it?
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="one-page-visual">
            <div class="page-frame">
              <div class="page-browser">
                <span></span>
                <span></span>
                <span></span>
              </div>

              <div class="page-content">
                <div class="editorial-side">
