                  <div class="visual-title"></div>
                  <div class="visual-title short"></div>

                  <div class="visual-copy"></div>
                  <div class="visual-copy"></div>
                  <div class="visual-copy medium"></div>
                </div>

                <div class="advertiser-side">
                  <span class="visual-label">ONE ADVERTISER</span>

                  <div class="brand-symbol">
                    <span></span>
                  </div>

                  <strong>
                    Contextually
                    <br />
                    Aligned Brand
                  </strong>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="visual-result">
              <span>ONE PAGE</span>
              <strong>One clear relationship.</strong>
              <span>ONE ADVERTISER</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="model-benefits">
            <article>
              <span class="benefit-number">01</span>
              <h3>Contextually Matched</h3>
              <p>
                A relevant advertiser is aligned with the subject and
                context of the editorial content.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span class="benefit-number">02</span>
              <h3>Clean by Design</h3>
              <p>
                No competing ad units. No battle for visual attention.
                Content remains the primary experience.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span class="benefit-number">03</span>
              <h3>Less Complexity</h3>
              <p>
                Reducing advertising components creates the potential
                for a simpler, lighter page architecture.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span class="benefit-number">04</span>
              <h3>Respect for Attention</h3>
              <p>
                Advertising becomes a relevant brand experience rather
                than an interruption users need to fight.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="model-statement">
            <span>THE PRINCIPLE</span>

            <p>
              Fewer ads do not necessarily mean less value.
            </p>

            <strong>
              Better alignment can create more value from one advertiser.
            </strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="case-study" class="section poc">
