      <section id="agentic" class="section collaboration-section">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="collaboration-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">06 — Agentic Advertising</p>

              <h2 class="section-title">
                Bringing Brand Integrity
                <br />
                to the Agentic Advertising Ecosystem
              </h2>
            </div>

            <p class="collaboration-intro">
              Agentic advertising will require more than interoperability.
              It will require mechanisms for evaluating <strong>who is acting, how they behave, and whether the data
              they rely on can be verified.</strong>
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="aamp-relationship">
            <div class="aamp-side">
              <span class="relationship-label">AAMP</span>

              <h3>
                Agentic Advertising
                <br />
                Management Protocols
              </h3>

              <p>
                AAMP is establishing an interoperable foundation for
                advertising agents to discover, communicate, negotiate,
                transact, and exchange signals across the advertising ecosystem.
              </p>

              <div class="relationship-question">
                <span>THE QUESTION</span>
                <strong>
                  How do advertising agents interact?
                </strong>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="relationship-bridge" aria-hidden="true">
              <span>+</span>
            </div>

            <div class="integrity-side">
              <span class="relationship-label">BRAND INTEGRITY INDEX</span>

              <h3>
                Integrity for Actors
                <br />
                and Information
              </h3>

              <p>
                Brand Integrity provides a complementary framework
                for evaluating the behavior of digital participants
                and the integrity of the information they exchange.
              </p>

              <div class="relationship-question">
                <span>THE QUESTION</span>
                <strong>
                  Can the participants and their information be evaluated?
                </strong>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="collaboration-result">
            <span>THE OPPORTUNITY</span>

            <h3>
              Protocol Interoperability
              <span>+</span>
              Behavioral Integrity
              <span>+</span>
              Data Integrity
            </h3>

            <p>
              Together, these layers could support an agentic advertising
              ecosystem in which automated systems can evaluate not only
              what information is exchanged, but also who stands behind it,
              what policies govern their behavior, and whether the information
              itself maintains its integrity.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="exploration-grid">
            <article>
              <span>01</span>
              <h3>Participant Identity</h3>
              <p>
                Explore how agents, publishers, advertisers, and other
                market participants can be associated with verifiable
                organizational identities.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>02</span>
              <h3>Behavioral Policies</h3>
              <p>
                Explore machine-readable declarations of authorization,
                operational policies, and expected behavior.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>03</span>
              <h3>Data Integrity</h3>
              <p>
                Explore how provenance and integrity signals can help agents
                evaluate content, contextual data, and other digital information.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>04</span>
              <h3>Brand Suitability</h3>
              <p>
                Explore how verified behavioral and data signals could support
                more transparent, policy-driven brand decisions.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="collaboration-note">
            <p>
              Y&H does not propose replacing existing AAMP protocols.
            </p>

            <strong>
              We propose exploring how Brand Integrity can become
              a complementary layer by design.
            </strong>
          </div>

          <div class="research-question">
            <span>THE RESEARCH QUESTION</span>

            <p>
              Can Brand Integrity become a measurable signal
              for agentic advertising?
            </p>

            <strong>
              We have a hypothesis, a framework, and early evidence.
              The next step is to test it.
            </strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

